1
00:00:00,306 --> 00:00:02,629
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,629 --> 00:00:05,095
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,095 --> 00:00:06,355
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,512 --> 00:00:08,856
I've been a surgeon for
twenty-eight years.

5
00:00:08,896 --> 00:00:10,516
Standing at the operating
table

6
00:00:10,516 --> 00:00:12,177
for hours at a time,

7
00:00:12,177 --> 00:00:14,113
long cases on my feet,

8
00:00:14,113 --> 00:00:15,000
getting called back

9
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,284
in the middle of the night

10
00:00:16,284 --> 00:00:18,460
more times than I could
ever count.

11
00:00:18,832 --> 00:00:19,912
That's a lot of years

12
00:00:19,912 --> 00:00:21,064
on a pair of knees.

13
00:00:21,104 --> 00:00:21,940
I had my right knee

14
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:23,464
replaced two years ago.

15
00:00:23,583 --> 00:00:25,315
It has hurt every day
since.

16
00:00:25,396 --> 00:00:26,698
Not surgery pain.

17
00:00:26,738 --> 00:00:27,920
I know what that felt
like,

18
00:00:27,920 --> 00:00:28,731
and it went away.

19
00:00:28,771 --> 00:00:29,893
This is different.

20
00:00:30,043 --> 00:00:30,724
Tight.

21
00:00:30,855 --> 00:00:31,506
Full.

22
00:00:31,756 --> 00:00:32,648
Like a band around

23
00:00:32,648 --> 00:00:34,401
the joint that never
loosens.

24
00:00:34,441 --> 00:00:35,643
And for two years

25
00:00:35,643 --> 00:00:37,135
I've been told the same
thing.

26
00:00:37,266 --> 00:00:38,177
Give it time.

27
00:00:38,398 --> 00:00:39,860
At six weeks it was
swelling,

28
00:00:39,860 --> 00:00:41,122
and swelling is normal.

29
00:00:41,162 --> 00:00:42,164
At three months,

30
00:00:42,164 --> 00:00:43,226
give it six.

31
00:00:43,316 --> 00:00:44,027
At six months,

32
00:00:44,027 --> 00:00:45,580
some knees take a full
year.

33
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:46,351
At a year,

34
00:00:46,351 --> 00:00:48,224
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

35
00:00:48,755 --> 00:00:49,977
And I didn't just wait.

36
00:00:50,308 --> 00:00:51,841
We went down the list.

37
00:00:51,881 --> 00:00:53,233
More physical therapy.

38
00:00:53,273 --> 00:00:54,134
Every session,

39
00:00:54,134 --> 00:00:55,627
every exercise at home.

40
00:00:55,797 --> 00:00:56,919
I got stronger.

41
00:00:56,959 --> 00:00:58,491
The tightness never moved.

42
00:00:58,662 --> 00:00:59,974
The pain pills helped,

43
00:00:59,974 --> 00:01:01,196
and that was the problem.

44
00:01:01,397 --> 00:01:03,340
I'm already on enough
every morning,

45
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:04,322
and nobody could tell me

46
00:01:04,322 --> 00:01:05,523
when I'd get to stop.

47
00:01:05,844 --> 00:01:07,006
Then a nerve block.

48
00:01:07,076 --> 00:01:08,729
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

49
00:01:08,769 --> 00:01:10,082
And after that, a second

50
00:01:10,082 --> 00:01:11,173
operation to go back

51
00:01:11,173 --> 00:01:12,595
in and do it over.

52
00:01:12,776 --> 00:01:13,687
I said no.

53
00:01:13,798 --> 00:01:16,202
Every morning I pulled on
my scrubs

54
00:01:16,202 --> 00:01:17,191
and my knee felt like

55
00:01:17,191 --> 00:01:19,015
a band was wrapped around
it,

56
00:01:19,015 --> 00:01:21,365
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

57
00:01:21,807 --> 00:01:23,957
Every morning I took
something for it

58
00:01:23,957 --> 00:01:25,563
and went in to the
hospital.

59
00:01:25,719 --> 00:01:27,281
Couldn't do the stairs,

60
00:01:27,281 --> 00:01:28,363
couldn't stand at the
counter

61
00:01:28,363 --> 00:01:29,926
long enough to finish
dinner,

62
00:01:29,926 --> 00:01:31,458
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

63
00:01:31,458 --> 00:01:33,692
game without shifting
every two minutes.

64
00:01:33,822 --> 00:01:35,295
It woke me at night,

65
00:01:35,295 --> 00:01:37,679
and it turned ordinary
things,

66
00:01:37,679 --> 00:01:39,302
like getting in the car

67
00:01:39,302 --> 00:01:40,884
or up off the couch,

68
00:01:40,884 --> 00:01:41,946
into a decision.

69
00:01:42,016 --> 00:01:43,328
After a long and serious

70
00:01:43,328 --> 00:01:44,641
talk with my wife,

71
00:01:44,641 --> 00:01:46,463
I went back in one more
time.

72
00:01:46,874 --> 00:01:48,026
That was the fourth set

73
00:01:48,026 --> 00:01:49,739
of X-rays on this knee.

74
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:51,603
And like the three before
it,

75
00:01:51,603 --> 00:01:54,006
the answer was everything
looks great.

76
00:01:54,067 --> 00:01:55,790
No loosening, no
infection,

77
00:01:55,790 --> 00:01:56,561
nothing wrong.

78
00:01:56,811 --> 00:01:57,653
Only this time there

79
00:01:57,653 --> 00:01:58,844
was no new number.

80
00:01:59,055 --> 00:02:00,127
Nobody said

81
00:02:00,127 --> 00:02:01,359
give it another six
months.

82
00:02:01,399 --> 00:02:03,022
There was nothing left to
give it.

83
00:02:03,272 --> 00:02:04,084
I sat in the parking

84
00:02:04,084 --> 00:02:05,005
lot for a while.

85
00:02:05,336 --> 00:02:06,608
Okay, I thought.

86
00:02:06,848 --> 00:02:08,130
Then explain this.

87
00:02:08,441 --> 00:02:10,324
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

88
00:02:10,324 --> 00:02:11,679
I hit my breaking point.

89
00:02:11,719 --> 00:02:13,559
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

90
00:02:14,012 --> 00:02:15,163
I'd just come home

91
00:02:15,163 --> 00:02:16,952
from a long night on call.

92
00:02:17,121 --> 00:02:19,034
Everyone in the house was
asleep

93
00:02:19,034 --> 00:02:20,667
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

94
00:02:20,667 --> 00:02:21,879
with my leg up,

95
00:02:21,879 --> 00:02:23,381
trying to find any angle
where

96
00:02:23,381 --> 00:02:24,503
it didn't feel like
something

97
00:02:24,503 --> 00:02:25,956
was wrapped around my knee

98
00:02:25,956 --> 00:02:26,767
and tightening.

99
00:02:26,997 --> 00:02:29,191
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

100
00:02:29,331 --> 00:02:31,114
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

101
00:02:31,545 --> 00:02:32,507
And I just thought,

102
00:02:32,507 --> 00:02:34,179
is this really my life
now?

103
00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:35,852
I can't live like this.

104
00:02:36,043 --> 00:02:37,895
So I made myself a
promise.

105
00:02:37,956 --> 00:02:38,807
I wouldn't go a day

106
00:02:38,807 --> 00:02:40,330
without looking for an
answer.

107
00:02:40,610 --> 00:02:42,203
And when I found one,

108
00:02:42,203 --> 00:02:44,086
I'd share it with everyone

109
00:02:44,086 --> 00:02:45,488
going through the same
thing.

110
00:02:45,980 --> 00:02:47,091
So I got my laptop

111
00:02:47,091 --> 00:02:48,694
out and went looking.

112
00:02:49,005 --> 00:02:50,226
Not for a product.

113
00:02:50,367 --> 00:02:51,579
For an explanation.

114
00:02:51,880 --> 00:02:53,562
Mayo Clinic forums,

115
00:02:53,562 --> 00:02:55,676
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

116
00:02:55,676 --> 00:02:58,260
doctor videos, medical
animations.

117
00:02:58,341 --> 00:02:59,272
And that's when I found

118
00:02:59,272 --> 00:03:01,075
a video from a physical
therapist

119
00:03:01,075 --> 00:03:01,566
named Dr.

120
00:03:01,606 --> 00:03:03,620
Steven Salinger, whose own
wife

121
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:05,522
had been through exactly
this.

122
00:03:05,663 --> 00:03:07,847
But before I say anything
else,

123
00:03:07,847 --> 00:03:09,469
I want to be straight with
you.

124
00:03:09,650 --> 00:03:11,933
You've already had
something work fast.

125
00:03:12,054 --> 00:03:12,935
The ice.

126
00:03:12,996 --> 00:03:14,568
The first week of a new
pill.

127
00:03:14,628 --> 00:03:16,441
The good day after a
session.

128
00:03:16,552 --> 00:03:17,603
Then it wore off.

129
00:03:17,643 --> 00:03:19,957
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

130
00:03:20,248 --> 00:03:22,321
Fast relief isn't relief.

131
00:03:22,361 --> 00:03:23,413
It's a preview.

132
00:03:23,674 --> 00:03:24,695
So I'm not going to tell

133
00:03:24,695 --> 00:03:26,107
you this works fast.

134
00:03:26,148 --> 00:03:27,089
It doesn't.

135
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:29,193
But if you're willing to
be patient,

136
00:03:29,193 --> 00:03:29,924
and to look at what's

137
00:03:29,924 --> 00:03:31,217
going on around your new
knee

138
00:03:31,217 --> 00:03:32,819
instead of inside it,
there

139
00:03:32,819 --> 00:03:34,882
is a real reason it still
hurts.

140
00:03:35,033 --> 00:03:36,695
And something you can do
about it.

141
00:03:37,357 --> 00:03:38,659
Let me explain what he
said,

142
00:03:38,659 --> 00:03:40,092
because this is what
changed

143
00:03:40,092 --> 00:03:41,303
everything for me.

144
00:03:41,544 --> 00:03:43,347
He started with the
basics.

145
00:03:43,638 --> 00:03:45,140
A knee replacement takes
out

146
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:46,883
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

147
00:03:46,883 --> 00:03:48,256
in metal and plastic.

148
00:03:48,296 --> 00:03:50,319
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

149
00:03:50,319 --> 00:03:51,891
you had before the
operation.

150
00:03:52,142 --> 00:03:53,484
That part I already knew.

151
00:03:53,805 --> 00:03:55,147
But then he explained
something

152
00:03:55,147 --> 00:03:56,480
nobody had ever told me.

153
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:57,341
He said,

154
00:03:57,341 --> 00:03:59,034
think about a swollen foot

155
00:03:59,034 --> 00:04:00,135
inside a shoe.

156
00:04:00,727 --> 00:04:01,988
The shoe didn't shrink.

157
00:04:02,129 --> 00:04:04,343
Your foot is taking up
more room,

158
00:04:04,343 --> 00:04:05,785
so everything feels
cramped

159
00:04:05,785 --> 00:04:07,177
and tight and squeezed.

160
00:04:07,388 --> 00:04:08,280
Your new knee sits

161
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:09,792
in a limited space with
living

162
00:04:09,792 --> 00:04:11,635
tissue packed all around
it.

163
00:04:11,836 --> 00:04:13,699
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

164
00:04:13,699 --> 00:04:15,311
had to work through that
tissue.

165
00:04:15,532 --> 00:04:18,046
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

166
00:04:18,417 --> 00:04:19,869
At first that's normal.

167
00:04:19,949 --> 00:04:21,572
But in some people that
swelling can

168
00:04:21,572 --> 00:04:24,317
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

169
00:04:24,357 --> 00:04:26,220
And swollen tissue takes
up more

170
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:28,123
room than calm tissue
does.

171
00:04:28,183 --> 00:04:29,546
So when you bend,

172
00:04:29,546 --> 00:04:31,288
that tissue gets
compressed.

173
00:04:31,469 --> 00:04:32,641
When you straighten,

174
00:04:32,641 --> 00:04:33,923
it gets pulled tight.

175
00:04:34,214 --> 00:04:35,376
That's the band.

176
00:04:35,416 --> 00:04:37,759
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

177
00:04:37,810 --> 00:04:38,801
And you start being

178
00:04:38,801 --> 00:04:39,933
the one who says,

179
00:04:39,933 --> 00:04:40,755
you go ahead.

180
00:04:40,795 --> 00:04:41,966
I'll stay here.

181
00:04:42,167 --> 00:04:44,000
And that's exactly why so
much

182
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:46,154
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

183
00:04:46,394 --> 00:04:48,548
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

184
00:04:48,548 --> 00:04:49,560
around the knee.

185
00:04:49,600 --> 00:04:50,601
Worth doing,

186
00:04:50,601 --> 00:04:51,503
and I'd done it.

187
00:04:51,593 --> 00:04:52,965
It does nothing about
tissue

188
00:04:52,965 --> 00:04:54,127
taking up room.

189
00:04:54,258 --> 00:04:55,750
A nerve block quiets

190
00:04:55,750 --> 00:04:57,964
the nerve carrying the
signal.

191
00:04:58,264 --> 00:05:00,227
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

192
00:05:00,348 --> 00:05:01,971
But when that irritated
tissue

193
00:05:01,971 --> 00:05:03,584
finally calms down,

194
00:05:03,584 --> 00:05:05,046
it holds less fluid,

195
00:05:05,046 --> 00:05:06,508
and it takes up less room.

196
00:05:06,699 --> 00:05:08,051
Less room taken up means

197
00:05:08,051 --> 00:05:10,064
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

198
00:05:10,205 --> 00:05:12,078
That's what takes the
pressure off.

199
00:05:12,368 --> 00:05:13,861
After two years of this,

200
00:05:13,861 --> 00:05:15,473
it finally made sense.

201
00:05:15,804 --> 00:05:17,797
The problem was never the
new knee.

202
00:05:18,018 --> 00:05:19,851
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

203
00:05:20,031 --> 00:05:21,634
He calls it the squeeze.

204
00:05:21,704 --> 00:05:24,038
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

205
00:05:24,299 --> 00:05:25,371
I'd bought knee sleeves,

206
00:05:25,371 --> 00:05:27,154
compression braces,
creams,

207
00:05:27,154 --> 00:05:28,686
half of Amazon really,

208
00:05:28,686 --> 00:05:30,479
and all any of it gave me

209
00:05:30,479 --> 00:05:31,350
was an hour.

210
00:05:31,421 --> 00:05:32,332
I even looked at going

211
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:34,175
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

212
00:05:34,386 --> 00:05:36,179
But at $200 a session

213
00:05:36,179 --> 00:05:38,423
with nothing covered by
insurance,

214
00:05:38,423 --> 00:05:39,805
that was a quick no.

215
00:05:40,106 --> 00:05:41,187
Then one night I went

216
00:05:41,187 --> 00:05:42,560
back to that knee
replacement

217
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:44,393
group and actually read
it.

218
00:05:44,523 --> 00:05:45,865
Thousands of people,

219
00:05:45,865 --> 00:05:47,648
years out from surgery,

220
00:05:47,648 --> 00:05:50,243
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

221
00:05:50,243 --> 00:05:51,655
nobody could explain.

222
00:05:51,946 --> 00:05:53,629
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

223
00:05:53,629 --> 00:05:55,712
the same thing kept coming
up.

224
00:05:55,852 --> 00:05:57,305
This one device,

225
00:05:57,305 --> 00:05:59,769
and people saying it was
the first

226
00:05:59,769 --> 00:06:01,131
thing that made a
difference.

227
00:06:01,171 --> 00:06:03,185
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

228
00:06:03,185 --> 00:06:04,537
alright, here it comes,

229
00:06:04,537 --> 00:06:06,000
he's selling me something,

230
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,762
let me shut that down
right now.

231
00:06:07,913 --> 00:06:09,786
I'm only here because I
made myself

232
00:06:09,786 --> 00:06:12,160
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

233
00:06:12,160 --> 00:06:13,202
that if I ever found

234
00:06:13,202 --> 00:06:14,594
something that helped,

235
00:06:14,594 --> 00:06:15,636
I'd say so.

236
00:06:15,947 --> 00:06:17,639
It's called the KenRelief
Red

237
00:06:17,639 --> 00:06:19,152
Light Therapy Wrap.

238
00:06:19,302 --> 00:06:21,456
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

239
00:06:21,796 --> 00:06:23,129
It looked like the cheap

240
00:06:23,129 --> 00:06:25,753
knee sleeves off Amazon

241
00:06:25,753 --> 00:06:27,446
that did nothing for me.

242
00:06:27,656 --> 00:06:29,950
But I went to their
website anyway,

243
00:06:29,950 --> 00:06:31,112
just to see what all

244
00:06:31,112 --> 00:06:32,344
the fuss was about.

245
00:06:32,705 --> 00:06:34,538
It's the same red light
therapy

246
00:06:34,538 --> 00:06:37,593
clinics charge $200 a
session

247
00:06:37,593 --> 00:06:39,827
for, off machines that
cost

248
00:06:39,827 --> 00:06:41,600
fifty thousand dollars,

249
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:42,942
in a wrap you plug

250
00:06:42,942 --> 00:06:44,284
into the wall at home.

251
00:06:44,756 --> 00:06:46,598
Two hundred and forty
lights.

252
00:06:46,769 --> 00:06:49,103
Red at 660 nanometers

253
00:06:49,103 --> 00:06:51,667
and near-infrared at 850,

254
00:06:51,667 --> 00:06:54,011
run together for the
strongest effect.

255
00:06:54,242 --> 00:06:55,934
Four strength levels.

256
00:06:56,055 --> 00:06:58,098
A five to thirty minute
timer.

257
00:06:58,329 --> 00:07:00,081
Then I saw the guarantee.

258
00:07:00,162 --> 00:07:01,494
Ninety days.

259
00:07:01,684 --> 00:07:03,397
Results or your money
back,

260
00:07:03,397 --> 00:07:05,721
no questions, no store
credit,

261
00:07:05,721 --> 00:07:07,534
and you don't even send it
back.

262
00:07:07,845 --> 00:07:10,209
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

263
00:07:10,209 --> 00:07:11,811
days to change my mind.

264
00:07:12,172 --> 00:07:13,344
There wasn't much to lose,

265
00:07:13,344 --> 00:07:14,305
so I ordered it.

266
00:07:14,366 --> 00:07:15,658
Two of them, actually.

267
00:07:15,808 --> 00:07:18,052
Only the right knee was
replaced,

268
00:07:18,052 --> 00:07:20,116
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

269
00:07:20,116 --> 00:07:22,139
and I'd done it for two
years.

270
00:07:22,590 --> 00:07:24,623
The left one was carrying
the difference.

271
00:07:24,663 --> 00:07:25,244
When it came,

272
00:07:25,244 --> 00:07:27,428
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

273
00:07:27,428 --> 00:07:28,630
because I'd been let down
too

274
00:07:28,630 --> 00:07:30,222
many times to get excited.

275
00:07:30,513 --> 00:07:31,875
What I felt was warmth.

276
00:07:32,116 --> 00:07:33,809
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

277
00:07:34,170 --> 00:07:35,993
More like it was coming
from inside

278
00:07:35,993 --> 00:07:38,136
the knee and spreading
around it.

279
00:07:38,437 --> 00:07:39,428
And that was it.

280
00:07:39,499 --> 00:07:41,141
That was the whole
experience.

281
00:07:41,191 --> 00:07:42,424
When I took it off,

282
00:07:42,424 --> 00:07:43,315
I'll be honest,

283
00:07:43,315 --> 00:07:44,988
nothing dramatic had
happened.

284
00:07:45,238 --> 00:07:46,881
And after what that video
said,

285
00:07:46,881 --> 00:07:49,015
that's exactly what I
expected.

286
00:07:49,055 --> 00:07:49,786
What was different

287
00:07:49,786 --> 00:07:50,758
was that for the first

288
00:07:50,758 --> 00:07:51,860
time in two years

289
00:07:51,860 --> 00:07:53,202
I'd done something for my
knee

290
00:07:53,202 --> 00:07:54,243
instead of to it.

291
00:07:54,694 --> 00:07:55,736
Twenty minutes,

292
00:07:55,736 --> 00:07:56,898
in my own chair.

293
00:07:56,938 --> 00:07:58,932
No drive, no copay.

294
00:07:58,972 --> 00:08:00,995
They say twenty minutes.

295
00:08:01,226 --> 00:08:02,317
I did thirty,

296
00:08:02,317 --> 00:08:03,590
twice a day,

297
00:08:03,590 --> 00:08:05,502
lowest setting that first
week.

298
00:08:05,793 --> 00:08:07,205
I put it on the calendar.

299
00:08:07,286 --> 00:08:07,997
The first week,

300
00:08:07,997 --> 00:08:08,848
I couldn't have told

301
00:08:08,848 --> 00:08:10,461
you if anything was
happening.

302
00:08:10,692 --> 00:08:11,563
I tried not to get

303
00:08:11,563 --> 00:08:12,224
my hopes up.

304
00:08:12,264 --> 00:08:13,657
I'd had things help for a
week

305
00:08:13,657 --> 00:08:14,588
and then stop.

306
00:08:14,759 --> 00:08:16,011
But somewhere in the
second week

307
00:08:16,011 --> 00:08:17,092
I noticed I'd come down

308
00:08:17,092 --> 00:08:18,885
the stairs without holding
the rail.

309
00:08:19,016 --> 00:08:20,197
I hadn't decided to.

310
00:08:20,508 --> 00:08:21,510
I just did it,

311
00:08:21,510 --> 00:08:23,173
then stopped halfway down

312
00:08:23,173 --> 00:08:24,475
because I realized.

313
00:08:24,655 --> 00:08:26,258
By the end of the fourth
week

314
00:08:26,258 --> 00:08:27,360
I'd slept through the
night

315
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,732
four times running.

316
00:08:28,842 --> 00:08:30,185
I stood at the counter

317
00:08:30,185 --> 00:08:31,437
and finished making dinner

318
00:08:31,437 --> 00:08:33,029
without looking for the
stool.

319
00:08:33,380 --> 00:08:34,983
None of that is dramatic.

320
00:08:35,023 --> 00:08:35,995
All of it was gone

321
00:08:35,995 --> 00:08:37,126
for two years.

322
00:08:37,327 --> 00:08:38,960
A few weeks later my wife
asked

323
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:39,911
if I wanted to walk

324
00:08:39,911 --> 00:08:41,694
the long way around the
block.

325
00:08:42,075 --> 00:08:43,167
And for the first time

326
00:08:43,167 --> 00:08:43,968
in two years,

327
00:08:43,968 --> 00:08:45,130
I said yes.

328
00:08:45,300 --> 00:08:47,174
I wanted to understand
why,

329
00:08:47,174 --> 00:08:48,706
so I read the whole thing.

330
00:08:48,856 --> 00:08:50,549
It comes down to four
steps.

331
00:08:50,589 --> 00:08:51,260
One.

332
00:08:51,561 --> 00:08:53,314
The tissue around a new
knee can

333
00:08:53,314 --> 00:08:56,219
stay inflamed long after
surgery is over.

334
00:08:56,590 --> 00:08:57,280
Two.

335
00:08:57,511 --> 00:09:00,056
Inflamed tissue holds
extra fluid,

336
00:09:00,056 --> 00:09:01,097
so it takes up more

337
00:09:01,097 --> 00:09:02,339
room than it should.

338
00:09:02,570 --> 00:09:03,321
Three.

339
00:09:03,511 --> 00:09:05,154
There's only so much room
in there.

340
00:09:05,194 --> 00:09:06,726
Bending compresses it.

341
00:09:07,037 --> 00:09:08,540
Straightening pulls it
tight.

342
00:09:08,730 --> 00:09:10,253
That's the squeeze.

343
00:09:10,293 --> 00:09:11,024
Four.

344
00:09:11,335 --> 00:09:13,659
Red and near-infrared
light have been

345
00:09:13,659 --> 00:09:15,882
studied for calming that
inflammation,

346
00:09:15,882 --> 00:09:17,225
so the swelling and the
pressure

347
00:09:17,225 --> 00:09:18,436
can come down with it.

348
00:09:18,677 --> 00:09:19,679
In a randomized trial,

349
00:09:19,679 --> 00:09:21,252
patients given light
therapy after

350
00:09:21,252 --> 00:09:22,033
a knee replacement

351
00:09:22,033 --> 00:09:22,784
had less pain,

352
00:09:22,784 --> 00:09:23,746
less swelling

353
00:09:23,746 --> 00:09:25,339
and better early movement
than

354
00:09:25,339 --> 00:09:26,230
those who weren't.

355
00:09:26,611 --> 00:09:29,075
A 2025 review said the
same,

356
00:09:29,075 --> 00:09:30,237
and was clear the evidence

357
00:09:30,237 --> 00:09:31,208
is still limited.

358
00:09:31,325 --> 00:09:33,526
I probably sound like a
broken record

359
00:09:33,526 --> 00:09:34,948
to the people I work with.

360
00:09:35,166 --> 00:09:37,109
But after two years of
doing everything

361
00:09:37,109 --> 00:09:38,982
I was told and getting
nowhere,

362
00:09:38,982 --> 00:09:40,314
you have no idea what it's

363
00:09:40,314 --> 00:09:41,917
like to sleep through the
night,

364
00:09:41,917 --> 00:09:43,179
say yes to the walk,

365
00:09:43,179 --> 00:09:44,631
and get my life back.

366
00:09:44,882 --> 00:09:46,204
So take it from me.

367
00:09:46,254 --> 00:09:47,597
Don't spend another year
waiting

368
00:09:47,597 --> 00:09:48,628
for it to settle.

369
00:09:48,789 --> 00:09:50,371
Don't spend two hundred a
session.

370
00:09:50,762 --> 00:09:52,124
More than ten thousand
people

371
00:09:52,124 --> 00:09:53,276
with pain after a knee

372
00:09:53,276 --> 00:09:55,991
replacement have already
tried this.

373
00:09:56,181 --> 00:09:57,724
Some had it worse than I
did.

374
00:09:58,044 --> 00:09:59,186
You can get the KenRelief

375
00:09:59,186 --> 00:10:00,779
wrap from their website,

376
00:10:00,779 --> 00:10:02,402
with a discount link

377
00:10:02,402 --> 00:10:04,175
and ninety days to try it.

378
00:10:04,465 --> 00:10:06,329
If it doesn't do anything
for you,

379
00:10:06,329 --> 00:10:07,370
you get your money back

380
00:10:07,370 --> 00:10:08,582
and you keep the wrap.

381
00:10:08,773 --> 00:10:09,945
They only release so many

382
00:10:09,945 --> 00:10:11,036
at that price.

383
00:10:11,157 --> 00:10:12,519
If it's still there,

384
00:10:12,519 --> 00:10:13,451
get one,

385
00:10:13,451 --> 00:10:14,960
and stop the squeeze.

